1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,667
Business Case 03 begins when a candidate starts a version-bound job
application.

2
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:15,973
A valid application is linked to the correct candidate identity with
governed provenance.

3
00:00:15,973 --> 00:00:19,168
The governed record is APP-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:19,168 --> 00:00:25,558
The accountable actors are Candidate, Recruiter, Candidate Support,
Privacy Reviewer.

5
00:00:25,558 --> 00:00:35,142
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:35,142 --> 00:00:39,739
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:39,739 --> 00:00:48,015
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:48,015 --> 00:00:52,613
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:52,613 --> 00:00:55,469
Process 1, Candidate: Create recoverable draft.

10
00:00:55,469 --> 00:01:02,132
The action save profile and consent produces versioned application draft
in the Application ledger.

11
00:01:02,132 --> 00:01:05,464
Process 2, Identity Reviewer: Resolve possible duplicate.

12
00:01:05,464 --> 00:01:14,508
The action compare provenance and propose match produces safe match, new
identity or review case in the Identity ledger.

13
00:01:14,508 --> 00:01:17,364
Process 3, Candidate: Submit exact versions.

14
00:01:17,364 --> 00:01:23,551
The action validate and submit produces immutable application attempt in
the Application ledger.

15
00:01:23,551 --> 00:01:26,883
Process 4, Candidate Support: Correct or withdraw.

16
00:01:26,883 --> 00:01:34,023
The action request governed change produces correction or withdrawal
work item in the Case ledger.

17
00:01:34,023 --> 00:01:36,882
The actual product route is /hr/candidates/PER-DEMO-001.

18
00:01:36,882 --> 00:01:44,030
It presents candidate duplicate resolution and governed correction in
the surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:44,030 --> 00:01:55,944
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:55,944 --> 00:01:58,993
The seeded workbench follows record DUP-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:06,615
Its governed fields are Identity A, PER-DEMO-001 , Jordan Lee; Identity
B, PER-DUP-004 , J.

22
00:02:06,615 --> 00:02:18,811
Lee; Match signals, Verified email, phone suffix; Applications, 3
retained separately; Consent sources, Direct and event registration;
Proposed resolution, Link aliases; preserve source records.

23
00:02:18,811 --> 00:02:28,466
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

24
00:02:28,466 --> 00:02:32,468
With Recruiter selected, we perform approve safe field-level match.

25
00:02:32,468 --> 00:02:37,359
The guard requires minimum-necessary signals agree and restricted
evidence stays separated.

26
00:02:37,359 --> 00:02:48,920
The state changes from Review required to Matched with provenance,
records DuplicateResolved, writes to the Identity ledger, and creates
the handoff: Recruiter receives corrected identity projection.

27
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:53,532
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate ambiguous match.

28
00:02:53,532 --> 00:02:59,682
The prepared failure is Email matches but name and source ownership
conflict.

29
00:02:59,682 --> 00:03:10,444
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

30
00:03:10,444 --> 00:03:13,893
The owned recovery is Resolve with authoritative source.

31
00:03:13,893 --> 00:03:18,205
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

32
00:03:18,205 --> 00:03:23,810
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

33
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:32,864
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through duplicate-review accuracy and correction turnaround and
minimum-context next-actor work.

34
00:03:32,864 --> 00:03:34,995
Business Case 03 is complete.

35
00:03:34,995 --> 00:03:47,355
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

36
00:03:47,355 --> 00:03:52,896
A valid application is linked to the correct candidate identity with
governed provenance.

37
00:03:52,896 --> 00:03:57,584
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
